/*Q5.
You are developing a program to validate if a given year is an Olympic year. Create a Java program that checks if a year entered by the user is a valid Olympic year.

Your task is to write a Java program that takes a year as input and checks whether it is a valid Olympic year or not. A year is a valid Olympic year if it is divisible by 4.

Input format:
  - The input contains a single integer representing the year.

Output format:
The program displays whether the given year is a valid Olympic year in the following format:
  - If the year is divisible by 4:

    <year> is valid

  - If the year is not divisible by 4:

    <year> is not valid

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Valid when divisible by 4.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int year = sc.nextInt();
        if (year % 4 == 0) {
            System.out.println(year + " is valid");
        } else {
            System.out.println(year + " is not valid");
        }
        sc.close();
    }
}
